I love looking into (potential) phishing emails and determining what is malicious and what isn't. It's something I had to do on help desk a lot, and it's a puzzle I enjoy solving even today. 

https://blueteamlabs.online/home/challenge/phishing-analysis-2-a1091574b8

The provided information is just an email sample, with all the headers and such included.

What is the sending email address? 
Look for a From line.
From: Amazn <amazon@zyevantoby.cn>
This is already suspicious because that is NOT Amazon's domain.

What is the recipient email address?
Right below the previous line shows who the email is addressed to:
To: saintington73 <saintington73@outlook.com>

What is the subject line of the email?
And right below that is a common phishing subject line:
Subject: Your Account has been locked

What company is the attacker trying to imitate?
The sender is shown as "Amazn." This looks a lot like it's trying to say "Amazon" without getting into legal gray areas.

What is the date and time the email was sent? (As copied from a text editor)
Right below the subject line:
Date: Wed, 14 Jul 2021 01:40:32 +0900
We may need this later to track down what happened after the email was received.

What is the URL of the main call-to-action button?
Towards the bottom, there is a large chunk of Base64, as indicated by the line above the massive encoded text. (Look at the second chunk of Base64.) Decoding that reveals a lot of information, but here is what the question is looking for:
title="Review Account" class="mcnButton" style="text-align: center; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); line-height: 100%; letter-spacing: normal; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: none;" 
That signals that next piece will show where the "Review Account" button goes:
